  "notes": "University Park, no formal tracks. The HPA department catalog was already largely populated. Real bug avoided: picked 'CMPSC 203' over 'CMPSC 101' for the 'Programming/Spreadsheets/MIS' item, since CMPSC 101 has an uncompletable placement-gate prereq (MATH 21, never scheduled anywhere in this plan) -- same recurring pattern fixed for STAT 184/DS 200/ECON 106/SUR 121/STAT 240 earlier this session. Of the '9 credits from HPA 400-level electives' pool, picked HPA 442/444/446, all of which resolve cleanly against courses already in this plan (HPA 332, HPA 301W, ECON 102/STAT 200 respectively) -- avoided HPA 445, which needs ECON 302/315/323, none otherwise scheduled. 'HPA 395' (Field Experience/Internship, listed as a Summer course) is scheduled as a regular-term item since the engine paces by credit cap, not literal summer/fall/spring labels. 'Supporting Course' (30 credits total, 9 at 400-level, department-approved list) and generic GEN ED/Elective pools are modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. Real prereq-fix fallout: STAT 200 and its own pool-mate STAT 250 both now require MATH 21 (an unscheduled remedial-chain course, same pattern as CMPSC 101 above) -- HPA 446's own STAT 200/STAT 250/ECON 102 prereq is unaffected since ECON 102 is already scheduled Semester 1, so added STAT 100 (Statistical Concepts and Reasoning, no prereq, same STAT department) as a further fallback on this item instead of chasing the remedial chain; the item now resolves to STAT 100 (3cr instead of 4cr). Handbook verification pass: found a real, department-published 'Supporting Courses' page (hhd.psu.edu/hpa/supporting-courses) listing 250+ approved codes across six concentrations (Generalist & Pre-Health Goals, Health Services Management, Health Policy and Planning, Population and Public Health, Long-Term Services and Supports, Health Data Analytics) -- the page's own text: 'Courses other than those listed below may be used to meet this 30-credit requirement, but course substitutions require department approval.' This plan doesn't commit to one specific concentration, so rather than fabricate a concentration choice or transcribe the entire 250+-code, 40-department union (well beyond this plan's own departments list and this session's verification budget), wired the 7 generic 'Supporting Course' slots to the real approved codes that fall within departments this plan ALREADY loads (BIOL/CAS/ECON/PLSC/STAT/MIS -- all real, all sourced from the same page, ~68 codes) and the 3 'Supporting Course (400-level)' slots to the page's real HPA 400+-level codes, excluding HPA 442/444/446 (already separate required items elsewhere in this same plan) and HPA 490/495/496/497/499 (internship/independent-study-style; HPA 395 already separately models the internship). The plain (non-Supporting-Course) 'Elective' slot in Semester 7 is left as a generic free elective, not tied to this specific 30-credit requirement. CAS 175 (on the real page) has no matching entry in this app's own cas_catalog.json (a scraping gap, likely a retired/renumbered course) -- left in as an unchecked fallback option, same tolerance used elsewhere this session.",
